Definitions

"Software" means the Challenges plugin in source or binary form, including its
documentation, language files and every part of it, such as individual
challenges, settings and menus. Ports or translations of its code into another
language, platform or mod loader are modified versions of the Software.

"Official sources" means only the GitHub repository github.com/cyperia/Challenges
with its releases, and the Modrinth project page modrinth.com/plugin/challengesplugin.
Obtaining the Software through a tool that downloads it from an official source,
such as a server panel's plugin installer, counts as obtaining it from that source.

"Server" means a Minecraft server or a network of servers, including its proxy,
lobbies and every round, world or instance the Software runs on.

"Operator" means whoever runs a Server, together with its staff and anyone acting
on its behalf.

"Payment" means money or anything else of value, given directly or through a
third party, including in-game currency, items, ranks, donations, subscriptions,
memberships, votes, boosts, sponsorships and advertising.

"Content" means videos, streams, clips, posts, articles and other media that a
content creator publishes.

Permission

Permission is granted, free of charge, to any person to obtain the Software from
an official source and to copy, use, modify and compile it, only under the
following conditions. These conditions limit the permission itself.

1. No payment. No Operator may require or accept Payment, from players or from
anyone else, in connection with the Software. In particular, no Payment may:
a. be required to join a Server, round or world where the Software runs, or to
use any part of the Software, including through a paid whitelist, membership,
entry fee or tournament fee;
b. unlock, extend, speed up, prioritize, influence or otherwise improve anyone's
access to or use of the Software, including through perks that apply to the whole
Server, such as a priority queue or reserved slots;
c. give rewards, multipliers, statistics or other advantages for playing with the
Software;
d. buy advertising, sponsorship messages or other promotion within the Software
or within rounds played with it.
Roles such as staff or administrator may have more rights in the Software than
other players, as long as no role or right is obtained through Payment. A Server
may sell cosmetics or perks that have no effect on the Software, on joining it or
on gameplay with it, and that are not made for, named after or advertised with
the Software. Paying for one's own server hosting is not Payment under this
condition.

2. Content creation. Content made with the Software may be published and
monetized, including with sponsorships, advertising, subscriptions and
memberships. Visible credit naming cyperia.net must be given in or with the
Content; the in-game credit shown in the Content counts. Payment received for
the Content itself is not Payment under condition 1. As the only exception to
condition 1, a content creator may let only their subscribers or members join a
round, if:
a. the creator plays in that round personally and it is streamed live or
recorded for publication;
b. the Server is open only during such rounds; and
c. the subscription or membership is a general one of the creator's channel and
is not offered or advertised mainly as access to the Software or to a Server
running it.

3. No sale. The Software and any part of it, modified or not, must not be sold,
rented, licensed, sublicensed or otherwise offered for Payment, alone or as part
of a bundle, pack, template or setup. This includes servers, rounds,
installation, configuration, add-ons, presets, configurations, worlds and other
products or services made for or with the Software and offered for Payment.
General server hosting is not affected. As an exception, hosting providers may
offer the Software preinstalled or as part of a hosting package and pass it on to
their customers for that purpose, as long as nothing is charged for the Software
itself and cyperia.net is named where the package is offered. Any other paid
offer that includes the Software needs the consent of the copyright holders in
text form. Also as an exception, a content creator may pay someone to install,
configure or modify the Software for their Content under condition 2, as long as
the result is only used for that creator's Content and is not offered to anyone
else.

4. Authorship and endorsement. The Software must not be presented as one's own
work, and modified versions must state that they are modified. Nothing may
suggest that cyperia.net endorses, runs or is affiliated with a Server, Content
or offer.

5. Credits and references. No credit or reference to cyperia.net in the Software
may be removed, hidden, shortened, changed or replaced by any means, including in
modified versions, through the Software's own settings, its messages or language
files, or through other plugins, proxies or resource packs. This includes the
credits, the links and the beta challenges that are shown locked in the public
releases, together with their notes. Translating the text around a credit or
reference is allowed as long as its meaning and the name cyperia.net stay.

6. Copies. The Software must only be obtained from an official source. It must
not be published, uploaded, mirrored or passed on, modified or not, except:
a. to the Operator of the same Server, including its hosting provider, for
running that Server;
b. in a fork of the official repository on GitHub, as long as no releases or
compiled builds are published from it; and
c. in private storage that only the Operator can access;
d. by a hosting provider to its customers, as allowed in condition 3; and
e. by someone a content creator paid under condition 3, to that creator.
A copy received under a., d. or e. counts as obtained from an official source. Every
permitted copy must include this license.

7. Scope. Parts of the Software that the copyright holders have not published in
an official source, and parts marked in the Software as excluded from this
license, such as the code of internal beta challenges, are not licensed and
remain all rights reserved. This license applies to all versions of the Software
published by the copyright holders, including earlier releases. Rights that
someone already received to a copy under a license other than a version of this
license are not affected.

8. Contributions. By submitting a contribution, such as code, a translation or
an asset, to an official source, the contributor confirms they have the right to
do so and grants the copyright holders a non-exclusive, free of charge,
perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, transferable and sublicensable right to use the
contribution in every way known at the time of submission, in particular to
reproduce, modify, distribute and make it available to the public, also
commercially, and to publish it under this or any other license.

9. Breach. If a person does not meet any of these conditions, all rights under
this license end automatically for that person, for every version of the
Software. They are restored only if the copyright holders agree in text form.

10. Law and liability. This license is governed by German law, excluding the UN
Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. Mandatory consumer
protection of the country where a consumer lives is not affected. The Software is
provided free of charge and as is, without any warranty. The copyright holders
are liable only for intent and gross negligence, except where mandatory law,
such as the German Product Liability Act, provides otherwise.

11. Changes. The copyright holders may publish a new version of this license at
any time, and it applies to releases published after it. For earlier releases,
they may end this license with 90 days notice, published in the official GitHub
repository and on the official Modrinth page. After that, every version of the
Software may only be used under the license version then in force.
